IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sga2-nouns`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: s 76A -- the consequences of a company financing dealings in its shares: contracts void or voidable, the Court's orders,
-- the certificate that protects a person who relies on it, the offence of signing a false certificate and the defence to it, and the saving of other rights.
-- Layer 1. Whether a contract or transaction was made in contravention of s 76 is a fact the caller states (or derives with sga2-s76-prohibition.l4).
--
-- HOW THE ANSWERS READ. A legal effect that the section gives to a class of contracts ("are void") is a per-section answer (ruling E1, option C of 2026-11-04):
-- JUST TRUE for a contract in the class that was made in contravention of s 76; NOTHING for any other (the list is not closed, or the contravention element is unmet: fork F-A16).
-- A flat negative ("is not under any liability") is JUST FALSE where its gate is met and NOTHING where it is not. A "may" function gated by "where", "when", "upon" or "on being satisfied" answers
-- JUST FALSE when the gate fails (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c)); those functions are listed in group G1 (fork F-A6) with the other reading, NOTHING.

§ `Section 76A(1) and (1A): void contracts and transactions`

-- (1): the following contracts or transactions made or entered into in contravention of section 76 are void: (a) a contract or transaction by which a company acquires or purports to acquire its
-- own shares or units of its own shares, or shares or units of shares in its holding company or ultimate holding company; (b) one by which a company lends money on the security of its own shares
-- or units, or of shares or units in its holding company or ultimate holding company.
-- src:8104 | 76A.—(1) The following contracts or transactions made or entered
-- src:8105 | into in contravention of section 76 are void:
-- src:8107 | (a) a contract or transaction by which a company acquires or
-- src:8108 | purports to acquire its own shares or units of its own
-- src:8109 | shares, or shares or units of shares in its holding company
-- src:8110 | or ultimate holding company, as the case may be;
-- src:8115 | (b) a contract or transaction by which a company lends money
-- src:8116 | on the security of its own shares or units of its own shares,
-- src:8117 | or on the security of shares or units of shares in its holding
-- src:8118 | company or ultimate holding company, as the case may be.
@ref s 76A(1) (src:8104-8118)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 76A(1) kind of contract or transaction`
      `the contract or transaction was made or entered into in contravention of section 76` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(1) the contract or transaction is void` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 76A(1)(a) a contract or transaction by which a company acquires or purports to acquire its own shares or units of its own shares, or shares or units of shares in its holding company or ultimate holding company`
         THEN (IF `the contract or transaction was made or entered into in contravention of section 76` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "made or entered into in contravention of section 76" -- the element is unmet (split site (i), fork line F-A16)
    WHEN `s 76A(1)(b) a contract or transaction by which a company lends money on the security of its own shares or units of its own shares, or of shares or units of shares in its holding company or ultimate holding company`
         THEN (IF `the contract or transaction was made or entered into in contravention of section 76` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "made or entered into in contravention of section 76" -- the element is unmet (split site (i), fork line F-A16)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following contracts or transactions ... are void" -- the list is not closed with "only", and the subsection says nothing of any other contract or transaction

-- (1A): subsection (1) does not apply to a disposition of book-entry securities.
-- src:8122 | (1A) Subsection (1) does not apply to a disposition of book‑entry
-- src:8123 | securities, but a Court, on being satisfied that a disposition of
-- src:8124 | book‑entry securities would in the absence of this subsection be void
-- src:8125 | may, on the application of the Registrar or any other person, order the
-- src:8126 | transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1).
@ref s 76A(1A) (src:8122-8126)
GIVEN `the securities are book-entry securities as section 81SF of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(1A) subsection (1) applies to the disposition` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) "book-entry securities" the securities are book-entry securities` `the securities are book-entry securities as section 81SF of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 gives that meaning` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a disposition of book-entry securities"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of a disposition of book-entry securities and says nothing of any other disposition

-- (1A): a Court, on being satisfied that a disposition of book-entry securities would in the absence of this subsection be void, may, on the application of the Registrar or any other person,
-- order the transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1).
-- src:8122 | (1A) Subsection (1) does not apply to a disposition of book‑entry
-- src:8123 | securities, but a Court, on being satisfied that a disposition of
-- src:8124 | book‑entry securities would in the absence of this subsection be void
-- src:8125 | may, on the application of the Registrar or any other person, order the
-- src:8126 | transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1).
@ref s 76A(1A) (src:8122-8126)
GIVEN `the disposition is a disposition of book-entry securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the disposition would in the absence of subsection (1A) be void` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application has been made by the Registrar or any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(1A) the Court may order the transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the disposition is a disposition of book-entry securities` AND `the Court is satisfied that the disposition would in the absence of subsection (1A) be void` AND `an application has been made by the Registrar or any other person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a Court, on being satisfied that a disposition of book-entry securities would in the absence of this subsection be void may, on the application of the Registrar or any other person, order the transfer" -- a "may" function gated by "on being satisfied" and "on the application": periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c) ("when", "upon" count as "where"); listed in group G1 (fork F-A6), the other reading is NOTHING (the grant rule of 2026-11-12) {G1}

§ `Section 76A(2) and (3): voidable at the option of the company`

-- (2): subject to (1), a contract or transaction made or entered into in contravention of section 76, or a contract or transaction related to such a contract or transaction, is voidable at the option of the company.
-- src:8130 | (2) Subject to subsection (1), a contract or transaction made or
-- src:8131 | entered into in contravention of section 76, or a contract or
-- src:8132 | transaction related to such contract or transaction, is voidable at the
-- src:8133 | option of the company. The company may, subject to the following
-- src:8134 | provisions of this section, avoid any contract or transaction to which
-- src:8135 | this subsection applies by giving written notice to the other party or
-- src:8136 | parties to the contract or transaction.
@ref s 76A(2) (src:8130-8136)
GIVEN `the contract or transaction was made or entered into in contravention of section 76` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract or transaction is related to a contract or transaction made or entered into in contravention of section 76` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract or transaction is void under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (6) protects the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(2) the contract or transaction is one to which subsection (2) applies` MEANS
    IF `subsection (6) protects the contract or transaction`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (6)(b): "any such contract or transaction is not invalid, and is not voidable under subsection (2)"
    ELSE (IF `the contract or transaction is void under subsection (1)`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (1)" -- a void contract is dealt with by (1) and the subsection says nothing of its being also voidable
          ELSE (IF `the contract or transaction was made or entered into in contravention of section 76` OR `the contract or transaction is related to a contract or transaction made or entered into in contravention of section 76`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a contract or transaction made or entered into in contravention of section 76, or a contract or transaction related to such contract or transaction" -- the subsection says nothing of any other contract

-- (2): the company may, subject to the following provisions of this section, avoid any contract or transaction to which the subsection applies by giving written notice to the other party or parties.
-- src:8130 | (2) Subject to subsection (1), a contract or transaction made or
-- src:8131 | entered into in contravention of section 76, or a contract or
-- src:8132 | transaction related to such contract or transaction, is voidable at the
-- src:8133 | option of the company. The company may, subject to the following
-- src:8134 | provisions of this section, avoid any contract or transaction to which
-- src:8135 | this subsection applies by giving written notice to the other party or
-- src:8136 | parties to the contract or transaction.
@ref s 76A(2) (src:8130-8136)
GIVEN `subsection (2) applies to the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company gives written notice to the other party or parties to the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(2) the company may avoid the contract or transaction by written notice` MEANS
    IF `subsection (2) applies to the contract or transaction` AND `the company gives written notice to the other party or parties to the contract or transaction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The company may ... avoid any contract or transaction to which this subsection applies by giving written notice to the other party or parties" -- a grant whose gate failed {F-A7}

-- (3): the Court may, on the application of a member of a company, a holder of debentures, a trustee for the holders of debentures or a director, by order, authorise the applicant to give a notice or notices
-- under subsection (2) in the name of the company.
-- src:8138 | (3) The Court may, on the application of a member of a company, a
-- src:8139 | holder of debentures of a company, a trustee for the holders of
-- src:8140 | debentures of a company or a director of a company, by order,
-- src:8141 | authorise the member, holder of debentures, trustee or director to give
-- src:8142 | a notice or notices under subsection (2) in the name of the company.
@ref s 76A(3) (src:8138-8142)
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 76A(3) applicant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(3) the Court may authorise the applicant to give notice in the name of the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER applicant
    WHEN `s 76A(3) a member of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 76A(3) a holder of debentures of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 76A(3) a trustee for the holders of debentures of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 76A(3) a director of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Court may, on the application of a member of a company, a holder of debentures of a company, a trustee for the holders of debentures of a company or a director of a company" -- a grant limited to a named complement; the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork F-A17)

§ `Section 76A(4) and (5): the Court's orders`

-- (4): where (a) a company makes or performs a contract, or engages in a transaction; (b) in contravention of section 76 or related to one that was; and (c) the Court is satisfied, on the application of the
-- company or of any other person, that the company or that other person has suffered, or is likely to suffer, loss or damage as a result of (i) the making or performance of the contract or the transaction;
-- (ii) the making or performance of a related contract or transaction; (iii) the contract or transaction being void by reason of (1) or avoided under (2); or (iv) a related contract or transaction being so void or
-- avoided, the Court may make such order or orders as it thinks just and equitable against any party to the contract or transaction or the related one, or against the company or against any person who aided,
-- abetted, counselled or procured, or was, by act or omission, in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in or party to the contravention.
-- src:8144 | (4) Where —
-- src:8146 | (a) a company makes or performs a contract, or engages in a
-- src:8147 | transaction;
-- src:8149 | (b) the contract is made or performed, or the transaction is
-- src:8150 | engaged in, in contravention of section 76 or the contract or
-- src:8151 | transaction is related to a contract that was made or
-- src:8152 | performed, or to a transaction that was engaged in, in
-- src:8153 | contravention of that section; and
-- src:8155 | (c) the Court is satisfied, on the application of the company or
-- src:8156 | of any other person, that the company or that other person
-- src:8157 | has suffered, or is likely to suffer, loss or damage as a result
-- src:8158 | of —
-- src:8163 | (i) the making or performance of the contract or the
-- src:8164 | engaging in of the transaction;
-- src:8166 | (ii) the making or performance of a related contract or
-- src:8167 | the engaging in of a related transaction;
-- src:8169 | (iii) the contract or transaction being void by reason of
-- src:8170 | subsection (1) or avoided under subsection (2); or
-- src:8172 | (iv) a related contract or transaction being void by reason
-- src:8173 | of subsection (1) or avoided under subsection (2),
-- src:8175 | the Court may make such order or orders as it thinks just and
-- src:8176 | equitable (including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
-- src:8177 | all or any of the orders mentioned in subsection (5)) against any party
-- src:8178 | to the contract or transaction or to the related contract or transaction,
-- src:8179 | or against the company or against any person who aided, abetted,
-- src:8180 | counselled or procured, or was, by act or omission, in any way,
-- src:8181 | directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in or party to the
-- src:8182 | contravention.
@ref s 76A(4) (src:8144-8182)
GIVEN `a company makes or performs a contract, or engages in a transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is made or performed, or the transaction is engaged in, in contravention of section 76, or is related to one that was` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied, on the application of the company or of any other person, that the company or that other person has suffered, or is likely to suffer, loss or damage as a result of the contract or transaction, a related one, or either being void under subsection (1) or avoided under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a party to the contract or transaction, or to a related contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person aided, abetted, counselled or procured the contravention, or was, by act or omission, in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in or party to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(4) the Court may make an order against the person` MEANS
    IF    `a company makes or performs a contract, or engages in a transaction`
      AND `the contract is made or performed, or the transaction is engaged in, in contravention of section 76, or is related to one that was`
      AND `the Court is satisfied, on the application of the company or of any other person, that the company or that other person has suffered, or is likely to suffer, loss or damage as a result of the contract or transaction, a related one, or either being void under subsection (1) or avoided under subsection (2)`
      AND (    `the person is a party to the contract or transaction, or to a related contract or transaction`
            OR `the person is the company`
            OR `the person aided, abetted, counselled or procured the contravention, or was, by act or omission, in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in or party to it`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) the Court is satisfied ... the Court may make such order or orders as it thinks just and equitable against any party ..., or against the company or against any person who aided, abetted" -- a "may" function gated by "where": periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); listed in group G1 (fork F-A6), the other reading is NOTHING (the grant rule of 2026-11-12) {G1}

-- (5): the orders that may be made under (4) "include" (a) an order directing a person to refund money or return property to the company or to another person; (b) an order directing a person to pay to the
-- company or to another person a specified amount of the loss or damage suffered; (c) an order directing a person to indemnify the company or another person against any loss or damage that may be suffered.
-- src:8184 | (5) The orders that may be made under subsection (4) include —
-- src:8186 | (a) an order directing a person to refund money or return
-- src:8187 | property to the company or to another person;
-- src:8189 | (b) an order directing a person to pay to the company or to
-- src:8190 | another person a specified amount of the loss or damage
-- src:8191 | suffered by the company or other person; and
-- src:8193 | (c) an order directing a person to indemnify the company or
-- src:8194 | another person against any loss or damage that the
-- src:8195 | company or other person may suffer as a result of the
-- src:8196 | contract or transaction or as a result of the contract or
-- src:8197 | transaction being or having become void.
@ref s 76A(5) (src:8184-8197)
GIVEN `the order` IS A `s 76A(5) order of the Court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(5) the order is one of the orders mentioned in subsection (5)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the order`
    WHEN `s 76A(5)(a) an order directing a person to refund money or return property to the company or to another person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 76A(5)(b) an order directing a person to pay to the company or to another person a specified amount of the loss or damage suffered` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 76A(5)(c) an order directing a person to indemnify the company or another person against loss or damage that may be suffered as a result of the contract or transaction or of its being or having become void` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The orders that may be made under subsection (4) include" -- an open list; any other order is for subsection (4)'s own "just and equitable"

§ `Section 76A(6) to (10): the certificate`

-- (6): if a certificate signed by not less than 2 directors, or by a director and a secretary, of a company stating that the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) (as the case may be), inclusive,
-- have been complied with in relation to the proposed giving by the company of financial assistance for the purposes of an acquisition or proposed acquisition by a person of shares or units in the company or in a
-- holding company or ultimate holding company, is given to a person -- (a) that person is not under any liability to have an order made against the person under (4) by reason of any contract made or
-- performed, or any transaction engaged in, by the person in reliance on the certificate; and (b) any such contract or transaction is not invalid, and is not voidable under (2), by reason of the contravention.
-- src:8199 | (6) If a certificate signed by not less than 2 directors, or by a
-- src:8200 | director and a secretary, of a company stating that the requirements of
-- src:8201 | section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) (as the case may be), inclusive,
-- src:8202 | have been complied with in relation to the proposed giving by the
-- src:8203 | company of financial assistance for the purposes of an acquisition or
-- src:8204 | proposed acquisition by a person of shares or units in the company or
-- src:8209 | in a holding company or ultimate holding company (as the case may
-- src:8210 | be) of the company is given to a person —
-- src:8212 | (a) the person to whom the certificate is given is not under any
-- src:8213 | liability to have an order made against the person under
-- src:8214 | subsection (4) by reason of any contract made or
-- src:8215 | performed, or any transaction engaged in, by the person
-- src:8216 | in reliance on the certificate; and
-- src:8218 | (b) any such contract or transaction is not invalid, and is not
-- src:8219 | voidable under subsection (2), by reason that the contract is
-- src:8220 | made or performed, or the transaction is engaged in, in
-- src:8221 | contravention of section 76 or is related to a contract that
-- src:8222 | was made or performed, or to a transaction that was
-- src:8223 | engaged in, in contravention of that section.
@ref s 76A(6) (src:8199-8223)
GIVEN `the number of directors of the company who signed the certificate` IS A NUMBER
      `a director and a secretary of the company signed the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states that the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) (as the case may be), inclusive, have been complied with in relation to the proposed giving of financial assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is given to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(6) the certificate is one that subsection (6) speaks of` MEANS
    IF    (`the number of directors of the company who signed the certificate` AT LEAST 2 OR `a director and a secretary of the company signed the certificate`)
      AND `the certificate states that the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) (as the case may be), inclusive, have been complied with in relation to the proposed giving of financial assistance`
      AND `the certificate is given to the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a certificate signed by not less than 2 directors, or by a director and a secretary ... is given to a person" -- the protection in (a) and (b) is stated for that certificate only

-- src:8199 | (6) If a certificate signed by not less than 2 directors, or by a
-- src:8200 | director and a secretary, of a company stating that the requirements of
-- src:8201 | section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) (as the case may be), inclusive,
-- src:8202 | have been complied with in relation to the proposed giving by the
-- src:8203 | company of financial assistance for the purposes of an acquisition or
-- src:8204 | proposed acquisition by a person of shares or units in the company or
-- src:8209 | in a holding company or ultimate holding company (as the case may
-- src:8210 | be) of the company is given to a person —
-- src:8212 | (a) the person to whom the certificate is given is not under any
-- src:8213 | liability to have an order made against the person under
-- src:8214 | subsection (4) by reason of any contract made or
-- src:8215 | performed, or any transaction engaged in, by the person
-- src:8216 | in reliance on the certificate; and
@ref s 76A(6)(a) (src:8199-8216)
GIVEN `the certificate is one that subsection (6) speaks of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made the contract or performed it, or engaged in the transaction, in reliance on the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (6) does not apply to the person by reason of an order under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(6)(a) the person is under a liability to have an order made against the person under subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `subsection (6) does not apply to the person by reason of an order under subsection (7)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(7) Subsection (6) does not apply in relation to a person ... if the Court ... declares" -- (6) gives no answer, and (4) decides
    ELSE (IF `the certificate is one that subsection (6) speaks of` AND `the person made the contract or performed it, or engaged in the transaction, in reliance on the certificate`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) the person to whom the certificate is given is not under any liability to have an order made against the person under subsection (4) by reason of any contract made or performed, or any transaction engaged in, by the person in reliance on the certificate" (a flat negative, ruling N2 of 2026-11-04)
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the protection is stated for a person who relied on a certificate that subsection (6) speaks of

-- src:8218 | (b) any such contract or transaction is not invalid, and is not
-- src:8219 | voidable under subsection (2), by reason that the contract is
-- src:8220 | made or performed, or the transaction is engaged in, in
-- src:8221 | contravention of section 76 or is related to a contract that
-- src:8222 | was made or performed, or to a transaction that was
-- src:8223 | engaged in, in contravention of that section.
@ref s 76A(6)(b) (src:8218-8223)
GIVEN `the certificate is one that subsection (6) speaks of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made the contract or performed it, or engaged in the transaction, in reliance on the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (6) does not apply to the person by reason of an order under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(6)(b) the contract or transaction is invalid or voidable under subsection (2) by reason of the contravention` MEANS
    IF `subsection (6) does not apply to the person by reason of an order under subsection (7)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(7) Subsection (6) does not apply in relation to a person ... if the Court ... declares" -- (6) gives no answer, and (1) and (2) decide
    ELSE (IF `the certificate is one that subsection (6) speaks of` AND `the person made the contract or performed it, or engaged in the transaction, in reliance on the certificate`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) any such contract or transaction is not invalid, and is not voidable under subsection (2), by reason that the contract is made or performed, or the transaction is engaged in, in contravention of section 76" (a flat negative, ruling N2 of 2026-11-04)
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the protection is stated for a contract or transaction made in reliance on a certificate that subsection (6) speaks of

-- (7): subsection (6) does not apply to a person to whom a certificate is given if the Court, on application by the company or any other person who has suffered, or is likely to suffer, loss or damage as a result of
-- the contract or transaction (or a related one), by order, declares that it is satisfied that the person became aware before the contract was made or the transaction was engaged in that the requirements of
-- section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) had not been complied with in relation to the financial assistance to which the certificate related.
-- src:8227 | (7) Subsection (6) does not apply in relation to a person to whom a
-- src:8228 | certificate is given under that subsection in relation to a contract or
-- src:8229 | transaction if the Court, on application by the company concerned or
-- src:8230 | any other person who has suffered, or is likely to suffer, loss or
-- src:8231 | damage as a result of the making or performance of the contract or the
-- src:8232 | engaging in of the transaction, or the making or performance of a
-- src:8233 | related contract or the engaging in of a related transaction, by order,
-- src:8234 | declares that it is satisfied that the person to whom the certificate was
-- src:8235 | given became aware before the contract was made or the transaction
-- src:8236 | was engaged in that the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA)
-- src:8237 | or (10) (as the case may be) had not been complied with in relation to
-- src:8238 | the financial assistance to which the certificate related.
@ref s 76A(7) (src:8227-8238)
GIVEN `the application was made by the company concerned or by another person who has suffered, or is likely to suffer, loss or damage as a result of the contract or transaction or a related one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has declared by order that it is satisfied that the person became aware, before the contract was made or the transaction was engaged in, that the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) had not been complied with in relation to the financial assistance to which the certificate related` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(7) subsection (6) does not apply to the person` MEANS
    IF `the application was made by the company concerned or by another person who has suffered, or is likely to suffer, loss or damage as a result of the contract or transaction or a related one` AND `the Court has declared by order that it is satisfied that the person became aware, before the contract was made or the transaction was engaged in, that the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) had not been complied with in relation to the financial assistance to which the certificate related`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (6) does not apply in relation to a person ... if the Court, on application by the company concerned or any other person who has suffered, or is likely to suffer, loss or damage ..., by order, declares that it is satisfied that the person ... became aware" -- an exclusion introduced by "if", unmet (marginal reading (a), fork F-A18): JUST FALSE here means the exclusion has not been made out

-- (8): for the purposes of (7), a person is, in the absence of proof to the contrary, deemed to have been aware at a particular time of any matter of which an employee or agent of the person having duties or acting on
-- behalf of the person in relation to the relevant contract or transaction was aware at the time.
-- src:8242 | (8) For the purposes of subsection (7), a person is, in the absence of
-- src:8243 | proof to the contrary, deemed to have been aware at a particular time
-- src:8244 | of any matter of which an employee or agent of the person having
-- src:8245 | duties or acting on behalf of the person in relation to the relevant
-- src:8246 | contract or transaction was aware at the time.
@ref s 76A(8) (src:8242-8246)
GIVEN `an employee or agent of the person having duties or acting on behalf of the person in relation to the relevant contract or transaction was aware of the matter at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is proof to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(8) the person is deemed to have been aware of the matter` MEANS
    IF NOT `an employee or agent of the person having duties or acting on behalf of the person in relation to the relevant contract or transaction was aware of the matter at the time`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is stated for a matter of which an employee or agent was aware; it says nothing of other matters
    ELSE (IF `there is proof to the contrary`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of proof to the contrary, deemed" -- proof to the contrary has been given, so the deeming does not operate (fork F-A19)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (9): in any proceeding, a document purporting to be a certificate given under (6) is, in the absence of proof to the contrary, deemed to be such a certificate and to have been duly given.
-- src:8248 | (9) In any proceeding, a document purporting to be a certificate
-- src:8249 | given under subsection (6) is, in the absence of proof to the contrary,
-- src:8250 | deemed to be such a certificate and to have been duly given.
@ref s 76A(9) (src:8248-8250)
GIVEN `the document purports to be a certificate given under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is proof to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(9) the document is deemed to be a certificate given under subsection (6) and duly given` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document purports to be a certificate given under subsection (6)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is stated for "a document purporting to be a certificate given under subsection (6)"
    ELSE (IF `there is proof to the contrary`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of proof to the contrary, deemed" -- proof to the contrary has been given (fork F-A19)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (10): a person who has possession of a certificate given under (6) is, in the absence of proof to the contrary, deemed to be the person to whom the certificate was given.
-- src:8255 | (10) A person who has possession of a certificate given under
-- src:8256 | subsection (6) is, in the absence of proof to the contrary, deemed to be
-- src:8257 | the person to whom the certificate was given.
@ref s 76A(10) (src:8255-8257)
GIVEN `the person has possession of a certificate given under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is proof to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(10) the person is deemed to be the person to whom the certificate was given` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person has possession of a certificate given under subsection (6)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is stated for "a person who has possession of a certificate given under subsection (6)"
    ELSE (IF `there is proof to the contrary`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of proof to the contrary, deemed" -- proof to the contrary has been given (fork F-A19)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

§ `Section 76A(11) and (12): signing a false certificate`

-- (11): a person who signs a certificate stating that the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) have been complied with in relation to the proposed giving by a company of financial assistance,
-- when any of those requirements had not been complied with at the time the certificate was signed, shall be guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for
-- a term not exceeding 12 months or to both.
-- src:8259 | (11) If a person signs a certificate stating that the requirements of
-- src:8260 | section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) (as the case may be) have been
-- src:8261 | complied with in relation to the proposed giving by a company of
-- src:8262 | financial assistance and any of those requirements had not been
-- src:8263 | complied with in respect of the proposed giving of that assistance at
-- src:8264 | the time when the certificate was signed by that person, the person
-- src:8265 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:8266 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:8267 | 12 months or to both.
@ref s 76A(11) (src:8259-8267)
GIVEN `the person signed a certificate stating that the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) have been complied with in relation to the proposed giving by a company of financial assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any of those requirements had not been complied with in respect of the proposed giving at the time the person signed the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(11) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `the person signed a certificate stating that the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) have been complied with in relation to the proposed giving by a company of financial assistance`
      AND `any of those requirements had not been complied with in respect of the proposed giving at the time the person signed the certificate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person signs a certificate stating that the requirements ... have been complied with ... and any of those requirements had not been complied with ... the person shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element of the offence is unmet; the provision's own question (split site (i), fork line F-A5)

-- src:8259 | (11) If a person signs a certificate stating that the requirements of
-- src:8260 | section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) (as the case may be) have been
-- src:8261 | complied with in relation to the proposed giving by a company of
-- src:8262 | financial assistance and any of those requirements had not been
-- src:8263 | complied with in respect of the proposed giving of that assistance at
-- src:8264 | the time when the certificate was signed by that person, the person
-- src:8265 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:8266 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:8267 | 12 months or to both.
@ref s 76A(11) (src:8259-8267)
GIVEN `the person signed a certificate stating that the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) have been complied with in relation to the proposed giving by a company of financial assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any of those requirements had not been complied with in respect of the proposed giving at the time the person signed the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 76 penalty`
`s 76A(11) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 76A(11) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person signed a certificate stating that the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) have been complied with in relation to the proposed giving by a company of financial assistance` `any of those requirements had not been complied with in respect of the proposed giving at the time the person signed the certificate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 76 penalty` OF 5000, 12, TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- The prohibition derived from the offence (ruling N2 of 2026-11-04): a person must not sign such a certificate when any of the requirements had not been complied with. No time limit: only the act reaches BREACH.
-- src:8259 | (11) If a person signs a certificate stating that the requirements of
-- src:8260 | section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) (as the case may be) have been
-- src:8261 | complied with in relation to the proposed giving by a company of
-- src:8262 | financial assistance and any of those requirements had not been
-- src:8263 | complied with in respect of the proposed giving of that assistance at
-- src:8264 | the time when the certificate was signed by that person, the person
-- src:8265 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:8266 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:8267 | 12 months or to both.
@ref s 76A(11) (src:8259-8267)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 76A act`
`s 76A(11) a person must not sign a certificate that the requirements have been complied with when any had not` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 76A(11) sign a certificate that the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) have been complied with, when any of them had not`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person signed a certificate that the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) had been complied with when any of them had not"

-- (12): it is a defence to a prosecution for an offence under (11) if the defendant proves that at the time of signing he or she believed on reasonable grounds that all the requirements had been complied with.
-- Delegated defences (ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)): when the belief is not proved, the answer is JUST FALSE, worded "this section gives no defence on these facts", never "no defence at all".
-- src:8271 | (12) It is a defence to a prosecution for an offence under
-- src:8272 | subsection (11) if the defendant proves that at the time when the
-- src:8273 | defendant signed the certificate he or she believed on reasonable
-- src:8274 | grounds that all the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or
-- src:8275 | (10) (as the case may be) had been complied with in respect of the
-- src:8276 | proposed giving of financial assistance to which the certificate
-- src:8277 | relates.
@ref s 76A(12) (src:8271-8277)
GIVEN `the defendant proves that at the time of signing the defendant believed on reasonable grounds that all the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) had been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(12) the subsection gives the defendant a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF `the defendant proves that at the time of signing the defendant believed on reasonable grounds that all the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) had been complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence ... if the defendant proves that at the time when the defendant signed the certificate he or she believed on reasonable grounds" -- this section gives no defence on these facts (periods and defences ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); never "no defence at all"

-- (11) and (12) together: the person is guilty of the offence and the defence of subsection (12) is not made out.
-- src:8259 | (11) If a person signs a certificate stating that the requirements of
-- src:8260 | section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) (as the case may be) have been
-- src:8261 | complied with in relation to the proposed giving by a company of
-- src:8262 | financial assistance and any of those requirements had not been
-- src:8263 | complied with in respect of the proposed giving of that assistance at
-- src:8264 | the time when the certificate was signed by that person, the person
-- src:8265 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:8266 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:8267 | 12 months or to both.
@ref s 76A(11) (src:8259-8267)
GIVEN `the answer under subsection (11)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (12)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(11) the person is guilty of the offence and subsection (12) gives no defence` MEANS
    IF `the answer under subsection (11)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF `the answer under subsection (12)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence to a prosecution for an offence under subsection (11)" -- the defence is made out
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the person is not guilty under subsection (11), so there is no prosecution to defend

§ `Section 76A(13) to (15): relief, related contracts, other rights`

-- (13): the power of a Court under section 391 to relieve a person to whom that section applies, wholly or partly and on such terms as the Court thinks fit, from a liability mentioned in that section extends to
-- relieving a person against whom an order may be made under (4) from the liability to have such an order made. Section 391 itself is not in these ranges.
-- src:8281 | (13) The power of a Court under section 391 to relieve a person to
-- src:8282 | whom that section applies, wholly or partly and on such terms as the
-- src:8283 | Court thinks fit, from a liability mentioned in that section extends to
-- src:8284 | relieving a person against whom an order may be made under
-- src:8285 | subsection (4) from the liability to have such an order made against
-- src:8286 | the person.
@ref s 76A(13) (src:8281-8286)
GIVEN `an order may be made against the person under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(13) the power of the Court under section 391 extends to relieving the person from the liability to have an order made under subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `an order may be made against the person under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "extends to relieving a person against whom an order may be made under subsection (4)" -- a scope limit with no "only" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))

-- (14): if a company makes a contract or engages in a transaction under which it gives financial assistance as mentioned in section 76(1) or lends money as mentioned in section 76(1A)(b), any contract or
-- transaction made or engaged in as a result of or by means of, or in relation to, that financial assistance or money is deemed for the purposes of this section to be related to the firstmentioned one.
-- src:8288 | (14) If a company makes a contract or engages in a transaction
-- src:8289 | under which it gives financial assistance as mentioned in
-- src:8290 | section 76(1) or lends money as mentioned in section 76(1A)(b),
-- src:8291 | any contract or transaction made or engaged in as a result of or by
-- src:8292 | means of, or in relation to, that financial assistance or money is
-- src:8293 | deemed for the purposes of this section to be related to the
-- src:8294 | firstmentioned contract or transaction.
@ref s 76A(14) (src:8288-8294)
GIVEN `the company makes a contract or engages in a transaction under which it gives financial assistance as mentioned in section 76(1) or lends money as mentioned in section 76(1A)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other contract or transaction is made or engaged in as a result of or by means of, or in relation to, that financial assistance or money` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(14) the other contract or transaction is deemed to be related to the firstmentioned one` MEANS
    IF `the company makes a contract or engages in a transaction under which it gives financial assistance as mentioned in section 76(1) or lends money as mentioned in section 76(1A)(b)` AND `the other contract or transaction is made or engaged in as a result of or by means of, or in relation to, that financial assistance or money`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "is deemed for the purposes of this section to be related" -- a deeming that adds to the ordinary meaning of "related"; it does not say another contract is not related

-- (15): any rights or liabilities of a person under this section (including under an order of the Court made under this section) are in addition to and not in derogation of any rights or liabilities of that
-- person apart from this section but, where there would be any inconsistency, the provisions of this section or of the order prevail.
-- src:8298 | (15) Any rights or liabilities of a person under this section
-- src:8299 | (including rights or liabilities under an order made by the Court
-- src:8304 | under this section) are in addition to and not in derogation of any
-- src:8305 | rights or liabilities of that person apart from this section but, where
-- src:8306 | there would be any inconsistency between the rights and liabilities of
-- src:8307 | a person under this section or under an order made by the Court under
-- src:8308 | this section and the rights and liabilities of that person apart from this
-- src:8309 | section, the provisions of this section or of the order made by the
-- src:8310 | Court prevails.
@ref s 76A(15) (src:8298-8310)
GIVEN `the right or liability arises under section 76A or under an order of the Court made under section 76A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(15) the right or liability is in addition to the rights and liabilities of the person apart from the section` MEANS
    IF `the right or liability arises under section 76A or under an order of the Court made under section 76A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of rights or liabilities "under this section (including rights or liabilities under an order made by the Court under this section)"

-- src:8298 | (15) Any rights or liabilities of a person under this section
-- src:8299 | (including rights or liabilities under an order made by the Court
-- src:8304 | under this section) are in addition to and not in derogation of any
-- src:8305 | rights or liabilities of that person apart from this section but, where
-- src:8306 | there would be any inconsistency between the rights and liabilities of
-- src:8307 | a person under this section or under an order made by the Court under
-- src:8308 | this section and the rights and liabilities of that person apart from this
-- src:8309 | section, the provisions of this section or of the order made by the
-- src:8310 | Court prevails.
@ref s 76A(15) (src:8298-8310)
GIVEN `the right or liability arises under section 76A or under an order of the Court made under section 76A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right or liability is inconsistent with a right or liability of the person apart from section 76A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76A(15) the section or the order prevails over the inconsistent right or liability` MEANS
    IF `the right or liability arises under section 76A or under an order of the Court made under section 76A` AND `the right or liability is inconsistent with a right or liability of the person apart from section 76A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where there would be any inconsistency ..., the provisions of this section or of the order prevails" -- the subsection speaks of an inconsistency between a right or liability under the section and one apart from it
